=== PART S: the sandwich class on synthetic boxes (exact)
S1  threshold rule against brute force over the vertices of the box: 168 boxes of 3 to 12 states, both ends: largest deviation 6.7e-16 (must be < 1e-10); control, the equation with l and u exchanged at the same t: not satisfied in 168 of 168 (must be nearly all)
S2  the sandwich as the first-order class P(sqrt(l u), hub metric): max of 270 random functionals over the polytope by LP against the threshold value: largest deviation 4.4e-16 (must be < 1e-8); random members of the box satisfy every pair constraint: 45 of 45; control, one weight 1 % beyond its bound with another state at the opposite bound: a pair constraint is violated in 45 of 45 (must be all)
S3  stability: largest TV(mu, mu_f) - (t* - E_mu f) / gamma over the class, every subset, 24 cases (random and indicator observables): +4.26e-14 (must be <= 1e-9); populations: sup TV / Delta times min(P, 1 - P): 0.841, 0.364, 0.782, 0.852, 0.783, 0.838, 0.944, 0.919, 0.965, 0.887, 0.946, 0.691 (the bound: <= 1); control, half the constant: violated in 18 of 18 cases (must be positive)
S4  sandwich + one datum: least threshold value over the multiplier against the LP: largest deviation 1.6e-09 over 30 cases (must be < 1e-6); a threshold value below the LP at a random multiplier: 0 of 150 (must be 0); the datum removes 0.11 (median) of the width of the box's range from above
